1	//! File interception engine (T-11).
2	//!
3	//! Monitors file system operations on the endpoint using the `notify` crate
4	//! (see [`file_monitor`](file_monitor::file_monitor)).  Captures CreateFile,
5	//! WriteFile, DeleteFile, and Rename/Move operations and forwards them
6	//! as [`FileAction`] events through a Tokio channel to the event loop.
7	//!
8	//! ## Audit event pipeline
9	//!
10	//! The [`run_event_loop`] function is the integration point between the file
11	//! monitor and the rest of the agent.  It:
12	//!
13	//!  1. Receives [`FileAction`] events from the file monitor.
14	//!  2. Resolves the user identity from the process PID.
15	//!  3. Evaluates the action against the Policy Engine (via [`OfflineManager`]).
16	//!  4. Emits an audit event to the local JSONL log.
17	//!  5. Sends a [`Pipe1AgentMsg::BlockNotify`] to the UI when the engine returns
18	//!     a blocking decision.
19	
